{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"body":"## Root cause (investigation 2026-11-03, session a85e3cd3; ticket not claimed: fix needs an operator decision)\n\n**Observation**\n- Every uv-ecosystem Dependabot run since at least 2026-10-07 failed (31 in `gh run list`); github_actions and pip runs succeed.\n- Before the 0.13.6 pin: pin `==0.12.7`, Dependabot uv 0.12.18 (runs 37691368474, 38642411336, 39227361438), later 0.13.5 (40547457160, 40774291030). After: pin `==0.13.6`, Dependabot uv 0.13.5 (41206250625). So Dependabot was AHEAD of the pin for half the window. The failure is not \"0.13.6 is above Dependabot's max\".\n- Mechanism: Dependabot runs its single bundled uv (`ghcr.io/astral-sh/uv:0.13.5` in dependabot-core `uv/Dockerfile` on main today). uv itself enforces `[tool.uv] required-version` and exits 2 (\"Required uv version `==0.12.7` does not match the running version `0.12.18`\", run 39697889651). dependabot-core `uv/lib/dependabot/uv/file_updater/lock_file_error_handler.rb` maps that message to `tool_version_not_supported` (PR #14055).\n- Upstream: dependabot-core #13199 (open) is this exact issue; PR #13827 (open, idle since 2026-06-01) would install the required uv; PR #14581 (parse/update required-version) closed unmerged 2026-11-01. The dependabot.yml options reference has no key to pin, override, or skip the tool version.\n- Not obsolete: Dependabot has not reached 0.13.6, and matching only lasts until either side moves (dependabot-core bumped uv 6 times between 2026-08-12 and 2026-10-22).\n\n**Consequence for the acceptance criterion**\n- Any spec that works must contain Dependabot's bundled uv. `>=0.13.6,<0.14` excludes 0.13.5, so it would still fail (inferred from uv's specifier check; not executed under 0.13.5, since no 0.13.5 binary is on the host).\n- 4 readers parse the exact `==X.Y.Z` from `required-version`: `.github/actions/setup-uv/action.yml`, the Makefile venv preflight, `scripts/check_uv_pin.py`, and `tests/unit/test_worktree_python_pin.py`. A range means moving the exact pin to another single source and loosening uv's own native check for direct `uv` commands, which changes the pin's guarantee.\n\nDecision is pending with the operator; options are in the session report."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793753462987016001,"uuid":"9b598d5e-366b-488c-a68c-92cb47045c16"}